# Strategy parameters

Do not add constants used by signal/risk logic inside strategy implementations. Every knob belongs on the mode params object (`GridParams`, `BollingerParams`, `DonchianParams`) and is set in `*ParamsFor(trend, volatility)`.

Regime lookup tables (`GRID_MULT`, `ADX_MAX`, …) are allowed only as the mapping that **fills** those params. `evaluate*` / `evaluateGrid` / `evaluateBollinger` must read `params.foo`, not a module `FOO`.

```typescript
// BAD
const CHASE_ATR_MULT = 0.5;
const chaseFloor = lastSell.price - CHASE_ATR_MULT * currentAtr;

// GOOD
const chaseFloor = lastSell.price - params.chaseAtrMult * currentAtr;
```
